{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era","id":433319,"title":"Elevator Pitch a Dark Era","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-08T17:35:59-07:00","id":433319,"title":"Elevator Pitch a Dark Era","content":"Keep the pitch brief, just a game line plus historical era/geopolitical region and a few notes on influences and possible themes.<br /> <br /> If you like another poster's pitch, expand on it.<br /> <br /> My first pitch:<br /> <br /> Wheels within Wheels (Mesopotamia, 586-539 BC - Mage/Demon)<br /> <br /> &quot;The Babylonian Captivity as seen through the eyes of two clashing factions of Mages and their Demon allies.&quot;<br /> <br /> Israel: A nation deceived. Their patron god, YHVH, is not the omnipotent Lord of the heavens, but a being cast out of the Supernal by an alien invader known as the God-Machine. An elite cabal of Mages within the Priesthood manipulates the kingdom on behalf of the Alienated Archmasters Enoch, Moses, and Elijah in order to restore Him to His rightful place.<br /> <br /> Their plans suffered a setback with the Samaritan Schism, but Judah remained loyal to her purpose. The loss of the Northern Kingdom to the Assyrians was regrettable, but an acceptable loss given that they had abandoned their purpose.<br /> <br /> Then Nebuchadnezzar came and carried away the Judean nobility and Priesthood, just as Sargon had done to Samaria decades before. The Mages of the Southern Kingdom found themselves drafted into a war that has been raging for nearly two millennia, between the severed halves of the very being who usurped their God\u2019s place in the Realms Above. Assyria serves the God-Machine\u2019s mummified husk, exsanguinated and hollowed out by Nimrod\u2019s army when they stormed Heaven, while Babylon follows the mysterious Principle of divine fire which spilled from its Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Caught within the machinations of these rival empires and the insane god-monsters they serve, the mages of Israel and Judah communicate in dream-visions and coded communiqu\u00e9s inserted into official state correspondence between their host nations. Aided by the fallen servants of both God-Machine and Principle, they play a deadly game \u2026 with the survival of their nation, their way of life, and perhaps humanity itself at stake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-12-2015, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T18:55:26-07:00","id":433409,"title":"","content":"Meiji Werewolf (1890s Japan - W:tF)<br /> <br /> &quot;Picture Seven Samurai, but with werewolves.&quot;<br /> <br /> Meiji Restoration, Japan (1890s Japan): The extinction of the Japanese Wolf coincides with the end of the samurai as massive reforms in the government and military forcibly bring Japan into the modern era. Western ideas and technology bring new spirits that clash with those old kami used to generations of appeasement, and the Forsaken find themselves struggling to balance tradition with the inevitable march of progress. It is clear that Japan cannot exist as it once did in this new age, and that sentiment hits hard for the heirs of Father Wolf's murderers. Can tooth and claw stand before ranks of foreign rifles? <br /> <br /> (The clash of two worlds that, ultimately, cannot coexist; the death of traditions that can\u2019t survive as a metaphor for Father Wolf\u2019s murder).<br /> <br /> tl;dr Forsaken as ronin in a time of profound spiritual upheavel as Japan is dragged into the modern era by foreigners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:57:33-07:00","id":433555,"title":"","content":"Updated the original post with additional info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T22:08:07-07:00","id":433597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=433555#post433555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Updated the original post with additional info.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox, you do know that your proposed Era predates the Orders by a few hundred years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T22:20:20-07:00","id":433599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=433597#post433597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Paradox, you do know that your proposed Era predates the Orders by a few hundred years?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not. That actually makes things a little different. I'll fix it tomorrow, but right now I'm going to bed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T23:03:27-07:00","id":433615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=433599#post433599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did not. That actually makes things a little different. I'll fix it tomorrow, but right now I'm going to bed.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you check out the Dark Eras Kickstarter page, the full text of the base book is there; To The Strongest is Mage in the time of Alexander the Great, and explains the birth of the Diamond and the Seers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:02:21-07:00","id":434046,"title":"","content":"Game of Chess- Scramble for Africa (Mage)<br /> <br /> The great race has began. Europe has divided the &quot;Black Continent&quot; among itself, invading and occupying the land. While the locals has tried to defend themselves, the might of the Great Powers of Europe have the advantage. Belgium, France, Brittan, Spain, Italy, Germany and Portugal are the main players in the game, united at a single side for one cause- the richness and slaves of Africa. While mortals are the ones to play the game, the supernatural also finds itself lured into the vortex- many mysteries are hidden in those lands, from unknown monsters, powerful gods, hidden magics and buried treasures. Like the great nations, mage Orders also make uneasy alliances for the greater goal. Both the Diamond and the Pyramid are working together- one to find the secrets of the ancient world, another to conquer and destroy them- but in order to achieve any of that, they are better to submit the local Nameless, who fight to protect those secrets from the European strangers. Who will win that game? Who is playing against whom? What is the prize? And what would happen if the secrets of Africa have their own agenda in that game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:54:47-07:00","id":434165,"title":"","content":"Mine are elevator pitches for very short buildings. Both are for Requiem.<br /> <br /> Requiem at Home: London, 1942. As the blitz rages through the nights kindred huddle desperately together, hunting in air raid shelters and subsisting off a malnourished herd. With every night a new final death arrives - dominance is about survival in these times, not might.<br /> <br /> Black Blood, Black Nights: in the 8th century a new religion is sweeping the deserts of Arabia, and the prophet's inheritors seem unstoppable. But with the old ways withering and the blood and fury of the new washing them away, how can the dead continue? As they scramble to rebuild in a way that gives them influence in this new world, they are in turn hunted themselves by creatures of smoke: the Jinn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/33-nifara","name":"Nifara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar33_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T10:19:30-07:00","id":434185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=433615#post433615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you check out the Dark Eras Kickstarter page, the full text of the base book is there; To The Strongest is Mage in the time of Alexander the Great, and explains the birth of the Diamond and the Seers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I'll have to check that out, given Alexander's conquest of Israel and the possible implications for Wheels Within Wheels as a pre-Orders setting.<br /> <br /> I'm actually envisioning something really ambitious now, along the lines of making the Babylonians servants of the God-Machine itself (which is responsible for expelling the Old Gods from the Supernal, rather than the Exarchs,) and saying that the Exarchs are actually Mages from the lost Ten Tribes who were taken into Assyria. Have them actually ally with the exiled Judeans and the Demons to overthrow the God-Machine and imply that this is the (or *a*) Fall of Atlantis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T10:28:30-07:00","id":434190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nifara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=434165#post434165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Blood, Black Nights: in the 8th century a new religion is sweeping the deserts of Arabia, and the prophet's inheritors seem unstoppable. But with the old ways withering and the blood and fury of the new washing them away, how can the dead continue? As they scramble to rebuild in a way that gives them influence in this new world, they are in turn hunted themselves by creatures of smoke: the Jinn.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a fantastic crossover Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:25:17-07:00","id":434401,"title":"","content":"Yeah, okay. I'll throw out a bunch.<br /> <br /> How about some future/alternate Earth eras to start?<br /> ______________<br /> <br /> <u><b>Dreams of Mars (Geist/Changeling Mars 2150)</b></u><br /> The first Mars colonies were established in 2026, and others soon followed. Mining operations on asteroids and Mars became big business and the corporate concerns that oversaw them bloated under their weight. Earth started to run out of clean water and food about ten years later. Decades of political squabbling over the truth of any potential problems left a world devoid of solutions to those problems, and riots began. The same story of ages past played out before \u2013 war burst out, colonies stopped imports and exports, and people stranded in the reaches of space began to die.<br /> <br /> The Martians didn't.<br /> <br /> They buckled down and weathered the vanishing support with fortitude and perseverance born out of their frontier ancestors and they lived \u2013 thrived, you might even say \u2013 in the cold, red wastes. Gangs became tribes, and tribes warred amongst each other over dwindling resources, renewable energy materiel, and found ways to integrate ever stranger things into their bodies, to better stave off the terrible climate. A century passed, and signals from Earth came again. The companies that put the ancestors on the red dust came back and claimed ownership over the Martians and their tools, and the Martian propensity for war turned up.<br /> <br /> That didn't work out too well; the invaders held the ultimate high ground, and even with all their cybernetics and emancipated robots and reborn machinery, the Martians did not win the day. The companies came down and reprogrammed what they could, fixed what they couldn't, extracted hefty fees from the rebels, and locked down the colonies. Now mines and work camps are little more than prisons, and they make them more like that every day, shipping in new meat from Earth to grind up in the mines looking for gold and copper, ignoring the tribes living squalid existences in the dust.<br /> <br /> These corporate concerns sit in orbit in their glittering homes with terraforming implements and gases all sitting and waiting for the button to be pressed to turn Mars into a new Earth, but they don't because the bottom line says that would lose them more money than it would save. They set lights out and exercise periods and uniform requirements for employees on the ground and implement their decisions through ruthless robotic stand-ins. It's 2150 and it's same-shit, different-day.<br /> <br /> Maybe you died. You suffocated in the thin air, you got pulped by a mining machine, you were the last survivor of a Martian raid or a casualty of war. Whatever happened, you got back up, you just had something else in your brain that tells you to kill, to fight back, to let the Martian dead find their rest and their exaltation in war.<br /> <br /> Maybe you went somewhere you shouldn't have. You found yourself in a winding canyon during exploratory EVA, your ship crashed someplace it couldn't have, your adulthood ritual among the tribe went wrong, and you found yourself in some other Mars, someplace with canals and angry red weeds and Martian cabbage and you took water with strange things in the depths of the caverns or hiding amongst the sharp-edged ruins and you know that dream of Mars is still out there, and it wants to be let out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:14:00-07:00","id":434506,"title":"","content":"Name: God-Kings of the Crescent<br /> <br /> Gameline(s): Immortals/Mummy<br /> <br /> Era/Region: Ancient Mesopotamia<br /> <br /> Major Influences:<br /> <br /> - The Epic of Gilgamesh<br /> <br /> - The story of the Seven Sages<br /> <br /> - The Tower of Babel<br /> <br /> Themes: Corruption, the ethics of rulership, divine and mortal hubris<br /> <br /> Synopsis: After the collapse of the Nameless Empire, the people of Irem spread across the Middle, many settled in the land of Sumer, and began to form an empire. The Sumerian Empire was ruled by mighty God-Kings, seemingly immortal men who carried the powers of gods. In truth, these so-called Gods were shams, mortal men who had siezed immortality for themselves. Some are benevolent, some are cruel, but all must be wary, as the Arisen and their cults still hide in the shadows, plotting to seize the God-King's thrones for the glory of Irem. And what of the mortals caught between them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:30:02-07:00","id":434562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=434401#post434401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, okay. I'll throw out a bunch.<br /> <br /> How about some future/alternate Earth eras to start?<br /> ______________<br /> <br /> <u><b>Dreams of Mars (Geist/Changeling Mars 2150)</b></u><br /> The first Mars colonies were established in 2026, and others soon followed. Mining operations on asteroids and Mars became big business and the corporate concerns that oversaw them bloated under their weight. Earth started to run out of clean water and food about ten years later. Decades of political squabbling over the truth of any potential problems left a world devoid of solutions to those problems, and riots began. The same story of ages past played out before \u2013 war burst out, colonies stopped imports and exports, and people stranded in the reaches of space began to die.<br /> <br /> The Martians didn't.<br /> <br /> They buckled down and weathered the vanishing support with fortitude and perseverance born out of their frontier ancestors and they lived \u2013 thrived, you might even say \u2013 in the cold, red wastes. Gangs became tribes, and tribes warred amongst each other over dwindling resources, renewable energy materiel, and found ways to integrate ever stranger things into their bodies, to better stave off the terrible climate. A century passed, and signals from Earth came again. The companies that put the ancestors on the red dust came back and claimed ownership over the Martians and their tools, and the Martian propensity for war turned up.<br /> <br /> That didn't work out too well; the invaders held the ultimate high ground, and even with all their cybernetics and emancipated robots and reborn machinery, the Martians did not win the day. The companies came down and reprogrammed what they could, fixed what they couldn't, extracted hefty fees from the rebels, and locked down the colonies. Now mines and work camps are little more than prisons, and they make them more like that every day, shipping in new meat from Earth to grind up in the mines looking for gold and copper, ignoring the tribes living squalid existences in the dust.<br /> <br /> These corporate concerns sit in orbit in their glittering homes with terraforming implements and gases all sitting and waiting for the button to be pressed to turn Mars into a new Earth, but they don't because the bottom line says that would lose them more money than it would save. They set lights out and exercise periods and uniform requirements for employees on the ground and implement their decisions through ruthless robotic stand-ins. It's 2150 and it's same-shit, different-day.<br /> <br /> Maybe you died. You suffocated in the thin air, you got pulped by a mining machine, you were the last survivor of a Martian raid or a casualty of war. Whatever happened, you got back up, you just had something else in your brain that tells you to kill, to fight back, to let the Martian dead find their rest and their exaltation in war.<br /> <br /> Maybe you went somewhere you shouldn't have. You found yourself in a winding canyon during exploratory EVA, your ship crashed someplace it couldn't have, your adulthood ritual among the tribe went wrong, and you found yourself in some other Mars, someplace with canals and angry red weeds and Martian cabbage and you took water with strange things in the depths of the caverns or hiding amongst the sharp-edged ruins and you know that dream of Mars is still out there, and it wants to be let out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but think of the similarities between alien abduction experiences and Faerie encounters of old, and suggest that the Fae of Mars be depicted as the Grays, Nordics, Reptilians, Insectoids, etc of UFO lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:34:29-07:00","id":434564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=434506#post434506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Name: God-Kings of the Crescent<br /> <br /> Gameline(s): Immortals/Mummy<br /> <br /> Era/Region: Ancient Mesopotamia<br /> <br /> Major Influences:<br /> <br /> - The Epic of Gilgamesh<br /> <br /> - The story of the Seven Sages<br /> <br /> - The Tower of Babel<br /> <br /> Themes: Corruption, the ethics of rulership, divine and mortal hubris<br /> <br /> Synopsis: After the collapse of the Nameless Empire, the people of Irem spread across the Middle, many settled in the land of Sumer, and began to form an empire. The Sumerian Empire was ruled by mighty God-Kings, seemingly immortal men who carried the powers of gods. In truth, these so-called Gods were shams, mortal men who had siezed immortality for themselves. Some are benevolent, some are cruel, but all must be wary, as the Arisen and their cults still hide in the shadows, plotting to seize the God-King's thrones for the glory of Irem. And what of the mortals caught between them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Book of the Deceived has Sumer being contemporary with the Nameless Empire, although that's the recollection of an Arisen who may be misremembering things. Great concept regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:05:35-07:00","id":434627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=434562#post434562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't help but think of the similarities between alien abduction experiences and Faerie encounters of old, and suggest that the Fae of Mars be depicted as the Grays, Nordics, Reptilians, Insectoids, etc of UFO lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think less Earth UFO lore and think in terms of Heinlein and Bradbury's Mars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:08:55-07:00","id":434632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=434564#post434564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Book of the Deceived has Sumer being contemporary with the Nameless Empire, although that's the recollection of an Arisen who may be misremembering things. Great concept regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Did not know that. I haven't gotten to read through Book of the Deceived yet, though, so it wouldn't surprise me.<br /> <br /> I was gonna just make it pure Mummy, but then I remembered that 2nd Sight and Skinchangers got an era, and I thought &quot;Now, why did they leave out Immortals?&quot; Plus, I think Mummies and Immortals juxtapose nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:43:58-07:00","id":434737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=434632#post434632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Did not know that. I haven't gotten to read through Book of the Deceived yet, though, so it wouldn't surprise me.<br /> <br /> I was gonna just make it pure Mummy, but then I remembered that 2nd Sight and Skinchangers got an era, and I thought &quot;Now, why did they leave out Immortals?&quot; Plus, I think Mummies and Immortals juxtapose nicely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It's worth checking out since, for all that the Sumerians barely get two paragraphs, those two paragraphs have a LOT of really cool info in 'em. Apparently the Ki-En-Gir (Sumerians) were the first advanced civilization Irem encountered outside their own, and practiced a similar form of sorcery to the Shan'iatu, but without the use of Nomenclature. That is, before the Shan'iatu crushed their armies, captured their king, and tortured him to learn all his secrets.<br /> <br /> Now, this is, again, from the first-hand account of a Deceived, so it may not be accurate (we don't know what his Memory stat was when he wrote it :P) but it suggests that Sumer was a peer of Irem rather than its successor. And if they practiced similar arts, then perhaps they were the first Immortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T19:48:42-07:00","id":435151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=434737#post434737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. It's worth checking out since, for all that the Sumerians barely get two paragraphs, those two paragraphs have a LOT of really cool info in 'em. Apparently the Ki-En-Gir (Sumerians) were the first advanced civilization Irem encountered outside their own, and practiced a similar form of sorcery to the Shan'iatu, but without the use of Nomenclature. That is, before the Shan'iatu crushed their armies, captured their king, and tortured him to learn all his secrets.<br /> <br /> Now, this is, again, from the first-hand account of a Deceived, so it may not be accurate (we don't know what his Memory stat was when he wrote it :P) but it suggests that Sumer was a peer of Irem rather than its successor. And if they practiced similar arts, then perhaps they were the first Immortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, Immortals even offers the possibility that Blood Bathing was invented in ancient Babylon, so it's not much of a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T02:04:48-07:00","id":435479,"title":"","content":"The Sumerian people the Iremites encountered were LONG predecessors of the earliest known Sumerian kings we know of, or people whose writings we've uncovered. Irem FELL 3832 BCE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-10-2015, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T02:15:42-07:00","id":435485,"title":"","content":"Yeah, so basically proto-Sumerians as the Iremites are proto-Egyptians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T02:39:12-07:00","id":435499,"title":"","content":"The Babylonian Captivity one is interesting - I was considering doing Vampire/Promethean for that setting - expanding on the material from Ancient Bloodlines/Ancient Mysteries, while the captive (preyed upon by vampires) Jewish community ends up creating the first Unfleshed clay golems under the partial influence of Babylonian Tammuz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T03:02:12-07:00","id":435507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era#post433319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Israel: A nation of Mages. Ever since Moses made his covenant with the nameless Old God on Mount Sinai, the Levites have been Sleepwalkers, with the true rulers of the kingdom, the high priesthood, drawn from among the Awakened - who appear at an unprecedented rate among them. The Guardians of the Veil dominate, answering only to the Alienated Archmasters Enoch, Moses, and Elijah. Their plans suffered a setback with the Samaritan Schism, but Judah remained loyal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I specifically would not want to ever be the case in anything canonical. Solomon was a Mage, to be sure. But for it Prophets called him blasphemer, whose corrupt dealings with powers man was not meant to command (including foreign gods) led to the fall of the kingdom in the eyes of those who would compile the Tanakh in the Captivity period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-10-2015, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:50:06-07:00","id":435843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=435507#post435507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This I specifically would not want to ever be the case in anything canonical. Solomon was a Mage, to be sure. But for it Prophets called him blasphemer, whose corrupt dealings with powers man was not meant to command (including foreign gods) led to the fall of the kingdom in the eyes of those who would compile the Tanakh in the Captivity period.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all perspective, man. You look at it with your handy game books and say &quot;Why would one man be labeled blasphemer for being a Mage if the Prophets were Mages too?&quot;<br /> <br /> I say &quot;They labeled him a blasphemer not for practicing the Art, but for practicing it outside their approved traditions. There was a line in the sand that divided the Art into 'religion' and 'witchcraft' and Solomon crossed it.&quot;<br /> <br /> See, the covenant with the Old God whom we'll call YHVH established certain parameters.YHVH, when He ruled in the Supernal, had dominion over the region now occupied by Aether. This gave those touched by His hand a predilection towards Awakening to the Obrimos path and an absolute bar on Moros, hence all the trappings of Death (inferior Arcanum) being ritually unclean in Hebrew culture. Contact with corpses and menstrual blood (the result of a dead ovum) were anathema.<br /> <br /> So what did Solomon do? He trafficked with Necromancers for one thing. That pissed off the Priesthood and the Prophets to no end. He also swapped secrets with foreign Mages, which was taboo. The nation of Israel was founded in service to YHVH and He gave them all the magical lore they needed to do their job, including some stuff that nobody else knew. By sharing these mysteries with foreigners and bringing in the rites and practices of other traditions, he corrupted the very foundations of the Israelite Art.<br /> <br /> Then there's the fact that the Priesthood and the Prophets held to a tradition in which the practice of the Art, if not its existence, was kept behind a series of ever-more closed doors. The Tabernacle's courtyard was restricted to pureblooded Jews. Only Levite priests were allowed inside the Tabernacle proper. The highest practice (recitation of ha-Shem, the true Name of God) was performed only once a year, in the Holy of Holies, by the High Priest alone.<br /> <br /> Then Solomon hired a bunch of goyim to build the Temple and had the brass, as a non-Levite, to meddle in Priestly affairs, never mind bringing in altars to foreign gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-10-2015, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:06:43-07:00","id":435868,"title":"","content":"I'm with Glamourweaver with that. While Solomon wouyld be a mage, many of the later kings of both Israel and Judea weren't having any magical powers, and I'm not sure I like making all the Prophets being mages as canon. It just doesn't feel right. Also. making all the Israeli into sleepwalkers just sounds weird- it feels too close to CWoD: Gypsy, and no one wants to make Gypsy 20th Edition if I'm not mistaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:31:44-07:00","id":435904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=435479#post435479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sumerian people the Iremites encountered were LONG predecessors of the earliest known Sumerian kings we know of, or people whose writings we've uncovered. Irem FELL 3832 BCE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. So here's a thought. According to the Testament of Marco Singe, back before the Furies cursed mankind, those who grew old and feeble rested in &quot;the shadow of the Earth&quot; before emerging, rejuvenated, to start another life-cycle.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Purified are the result of an imperfect recreation of this natural process while the Arisen are that of a corruption of it, substituting the energies of Duat (Abbadonian Death/Matter) for those of the Shadow (Phenomenal Life/Spirit).<br /> <br /> The original process might have involved an infusion of pure Life energy, which the Purified, unable to recreate this process due to Death's curse, have substituted Spirit for, reasoning that they both come from the Shadow, so it's close enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-10-2015, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:27:47-07:00","id":436049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=435868#post435868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm with Glamourweaver with that. While Solomon wouyld be a mage, many of the later kings of both Israel and Judea weren't having any magical powers, and I'm not sure I like making all the Prophets being mages as canon. It just doesn't feel right. Also. making all the Israeli into sleepwalkers just sounds weird- it feels too close to CWoD: Gypsy, and no one wants to make Gypsy 20th Edition if I'm not mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>The KINGS of Israel, by and large, weren't Awakened, nor were the entire population Sleepwalkers (despite what I might have posted earlier; I have a tendency to post half-baked ideas and refine them later. Plus my understanding of WoD terminology is somewhat shaky at times.)<br /> <br /> Rather, the Levites in particular had a tendency to become Sleepwalkers and Awakened outright at an unprecedented rate, pretty much exclusively to the Obrimos path. Disbelief wasn't really a thing then either, generally speaking, throughout the world at large, since everyone pretty much believed in the supernatural.<br /> <br /> The Priesthood was dedicated to a specific purpose, however. They weren't like modern Mages, pursuing whatever mystical studies they pleased, but exactly what the Tanakh portrays them as: servants of YHVH. The Prophets likewise, though they could come from any tribe and were able to Awaken to any Path but Moros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:02:09-07:00","id":436079,"title":"","content":"It probably isn't a great idea to pin the Judeo-Christian God down as one of the Old Gods and a bunch of the prophets as Mages. Not only do you start getting into the whole &quot;Jesus was a vampire or possibly Lucifer, who was also Buddha&quot; that cWoD sometimes suffered from, but you also undermine a bunch of other splats, like the Malleus Maleficarum and possibly the Lancea et Sanctum. This is all before bringing the God-Machine or Principle into the equation either.<br /> <br /> This is a can of worms that should not be opened","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:09:54-07:00","id":436085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=436049#post436049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The KINGS of Israel, by and large, weren't Awakened, nor were the entire population Sleepwalkers (despite what I might have posted earlier; I have a tendency to post half-baked ideas and refine them later. Plus my understanding of WoD terminology is somewhat shaky at times.)<br /> <br /> Rather, the Levites in particular had a tendency to become Sleepwalkers and Awakened outright at an unprecedented rate, pretty much exclusively to the Obrimos path. Disbelief wasn't really a thing then either, generally speaking, throughout the world at large, since everyone pretty much believed in the supernatural.<br /> <br /> The Priesthood was dedicated to a specific purpose, however. They weren't like modern Mages, pursuing whatever mystical studies they pleased, but exactly what the Tanakh portrays them as: servants of YHVH. The Prophets likewise, though they could come from any tribe and were able to Awaken to any Path but Moros.</div> </div> </div> </div>about Disbelief- the number of people believing in the supernatural is not relevant for creating Paradoxes or using magic. The name itself is going to be changed at 2nd edition to avoid that confusion, if I'm not mistaken. This is the effect of the Abyss, and as long as that black void stands between the Supernal and the Fallen, magic may fail even if every single person upon Earth would believe that you can throw fireballs.<br /> <br /> Second, the bible doesn't forbid only Necromancers- but all kinds of magic workers. Many forms of Divination are included, and so are many other magical practices- no diviner, no enchanter, no witch, no charmer, no medium, no wizard, no necromancer, no cloud reader or astrologer. Going by Paths, then you have no Moros, no Acanthus, no Thyrsus, no Mastigus and maybe even no Obrimus. Unless you claim that the priests has decided to monopolize magic and worked to destroy competition, it would be weird to claim the Prophets as mages. Even if you decide they banned only Arcana, you won't have Time, Fate, Death, Spirit, Mind or Forces at the very least- which is harsh for a society of mages. Also, the prophets weren't the leaders of Israel- you can't count the number of times the Prophets raged that the people of Israel defied the will of God- but in the end, they didn't punished them or forced them to follow the rules. Those parts belonged to God and the Kings.<br /> <br /> In short, I think that while the idea could be interesting- it would require a lot of work so the Suspension of Disbelief would not be kicked out of the window- and that is without mentioning the screams about &quot;stereotyping&quot; and &quot;bigotry&quot; which may rise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:50:57-07:00","id":436178,"title":"","content":"Kind of agree with a lot of the others, though the idea of a secret Nameless Order within the priesthood of ancient Israel sounds like it could work. <br /> <br /> But, back onto topic. Here's my(probably pitiful) idea.<br /> <br /> BRAMBLES AND SHACKLES<br /> Game: Changeling<br /> Time: Civil War period, Southern US,1861-1865.<br /> Not to much I can say about it, I'm ashamed to admit. I'm just intently curious about how it might work. How do the Lost in this place deal with the war over a subject so close to home? Dig their heads in the sands? Fight for freedom, even if it means losing ties to the friends and loved ones they've worked so hard to regain? Or do they swallow their morals, join with the elite, and become no better than the monsters they escaped?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:55:44-07:00","id":436305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=435843#post435843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's all perspective, man. You look at it with your handy game books and say &quot;Why would one man be labeled blasphemer for being a Mage if the Prophets were Mages too?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I'm saying. I'm saying Priests and Prophets aren't Mages - because Mages wield agency over their power and Prophets do not. They just deliver messages from the force that wields said power and takes the supernatural actions on its own accord. Solomon is the only Biblical figure who traditions treat like a Mage. There may be others Awakened CLAIM, but it's going to be highly disputed.<br /> <br /> Also the alienated nature of the Awakened from society is kind of a fundamental theme in the game. They don't get institutionally elevated as a group.<br /> <br /> Any general presenting any real society as magically enlightened relative to others strikes me as patronizing and silly - not to mention touched with ethnocentrism. We elevate the Ancient Judeans because the dominant religion in our society claims them as forebearers. It's the same reason in any media portrayal of the Greco-Persian Wars in our society the Greeks are Good Guys and the Persians are Bad Guys.<br /> <br /> The Kohanim were a priestly bloodline, no different from any Indian Brahmin (which is to say, some individuals could be Awakened - sure, but it's not the nature of the group).<br /> <br /> I'm saying this as a Jew myself: Our ancient forebearers were not special in any way (outside of their relationship to YHWH in the context of our religion, but henotheists who believe themselves favored by their god are not unique or special in a global sense). Mage's cosmology is Gnostic - it in no way jives with the theology of Tanakh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-10-2015, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T15:41:21-07:00","id":436358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=436079#post436079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It probably isn't a great idea to pin the Judeo-Christian God down as one of the Old Gods and a bunch of the prophets as Mages. Not only do you start getting into the whole &quot;Jesus was a vampire or possibly Lucifer, who was also Buddha&quot; that cWoD sometimes suffered from, but you also undermine a bunch of other splats, like the Malleus Maleficarum and possibly the Lancea et Sanctum. This is all before bringing the God-Machine or Principle into the equation either.<br /> <br /> This is a can of worms that should not be opened</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=436085#post436085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> about Disbelief- the number of people believing in the supernatural is not relevant for creating Paradoxes or using magic. The name itself is going to be changed at 2nd edition to avoid that confusion, if I'm not mistaken. This is the effect of the Abyss, and as long as that black void stands between the Supernal and the Fallen, magic may fail even if every single person upon Earth would believe that you can throw fireballs.<br /> <br /> Second, the bible doesn't forbid only Necromancers- but all kinds of magic workers. Many forms of Divination are included, and so are many other magical practices- no diviner, no enchanter, no witch, no charmer, no medium, no wizard, no necromancer, no cloud reader or astrologer. Going by Paths, then you have no Moros, no Acanthus, no Thyrsus, no Mastigus and maybe even no Obrimus. Unless you claim that the priests has decided to monopolize magic and worked to destroy competition, it would be weird to claim the Prophets as mages. Even if you decide they banned only Arcana, you won't have Time, Fate, Death, Spirit, Mind or Forces at the very least- which is harsh for a society of mages. Also, the prophets weren't the leaders of Israel- you can't count the number of times the Prophets raged that the people of Israel defied the will of God- but in the end, they didn't punished them or forced them to follow the rules. Those parts belonged to God and the Kings.<br /> <br /> In short, I think that while the idea could be interesting- it would require a lot of work so the Suspension of Disbelief would not be kicked out of the window- and that is without mentioning the screams about &quot;stereotyping&quot; and &quot;bigotry&quot; which may rise.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=436178#post436178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of agree with a lot of the others, though the idea of a secret Nameless Order within the priesthood of ancient Israel sounds like it could work.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=436305#post436305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not what I'm saying. I'm saying Priests and Prophets aren't Mages - because Mages wield agency over their power and Prophets do not. They just deliver messages from the force that wields said power and takes the supernatural actions on its own accord. Solomon is the only Biblical figure who traditions treat like a Mage. There may be others Awakened CLAIM, but it's going to be highly disputed.<br /> <br /> Also the alienated nature of the Awakened from society is kind of a fundamental theme in the game. They don't get institutionally elevated as a group.<br /> <br /> Any general presenting any real society as magically enlightened relative to others strikes me as patronizing and silly - not to mention touched with ethnocentrism. We elevate the Ancient Judeans because the dominant religion in our society claims them as forebearers. It's the same reason in any media portrayal of the Greco-Persian Wars in our society the Greeks are Good Guys and the Persians are Bad Guys.<br /> <br /> The Kohanim were a priestly bloodline, no different from any Indian Brahmin (which is to say, some individuals could be Awakened - sure, but it's not the nature of the group).<br /> <br /> I'm saying this as a Jew myself: Our ancient forebearers were not special in any way (outside of their relationship to YHWH in the context of our religion, but henotheists who believe themselves favored by their god are not unique or special in a global sense). Mage's cosmology is Gnostic - it in no way jives with the theology of Tanakh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'm about as devout as anyone, but I can separate fiction from reality. Concerns about blasphemy don't bother me, since I'm proposing it all as a work of make-believe.<br /> <br /> Anyway, yeah, I was kinda looking at it in terms of ALL ancient societies being the product of some supernatural splat or another. I mean Egypt was the successor-state of Irem's Nameless Empire, which was the work of the Shan'iatu; Sumer was founded by sorcerer-kings who rivaled the Shan'iatu; my pitch has Assyria and Babylonia serving the God-Machine and the Principle, respectively; etc. So Israel doesn't become special except in the sense that they were specifically a nation founded by Mages rather than one founded by some other splat.<br /> <br /> The whole idea is that Abraham, Moses, et al, when they made their covenants with YHVH, got some magical mojo injected into the bloodline that allowed for a higher rate of Sleepwalkers and Awakened (originally this was to be nationwide, however the covenant was modified to restrict it to the Levites specifically). However, part of the setting would be explaining how Israelite Awakened are different from standard Mages - they are explicitly SERVANTS of YHVH, not the dilettantes of modern Awakened society.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind also that the Tanakh was probably compiled post-Exile and reflects a particular POV which may not be in line with the literal truth (speaking both in terms of the real world and the WoD perspectives.) We know that Israel was a bunch of stiffnecked, wayward children who frustrated YHVH to no end; the only reason He put up with them is because all the other nations were even worse. Any prophet whose preachings were unpopular was put to death and their writings were destroyed; and the Priesthood had a tendency to usurp political power instead of serving as they were supposed to.<br /> <br /> As to the prohibitions on divination, witchcraft, etc.: The holy men of Israel prophesied (Time,) cursed the enemies of the Lord (Fate,) discerned thoughts (Mind,) commanded beasts (Spirit,) and called down the power of the elements (Forces.) The difference between that and the prohibited practices? Well, if you're doing it according to the rules (by the power of and in service to YHVH), you're okey-dokey, otherwise (calling on foreign gods, communing with ghosts, going against YHVH's orders, etc.) you get stoned.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I think changing it to &quot;A lot of Levites were Sleepwalkers/Awakened&quot; rather than &quot;All Levites&quot; is a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-10-2015, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T16:27:34-07:00","id":436397,"title":"","content":"No one is arguing against your idea because it is blasphemous or anything. The problem is that it destroys more pothooks then it creates, makes being Jewish magic, and steps on a bunch of non-Mage toes. I'm not one to cry Mage Supremacy, but here lies the way of Mage Supremacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T20:03:54-07:00","id":436596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=436397#post436397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is arguing against your idea because it is blasphemous or anything. The problem is that it destroys more pothooks then it creates, makes being Jewish magic, and steps on a bunch of non-Mage toes. I'm not one to cry Mage Supremacy, but here lies the way of Mage Supremacy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This - exactly this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T21:04:18-07:00","id":436641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=436596#post436596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This - exactly this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I'ma let the idea bake for a while and bring it back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T03:27:12-07:00","id":436871,"title":"","content":"Setting: Carthage, 520-34ish AD<br /> Gameline: Geist/Mummy Crossover<br /> Theme: On the Edge of the World<br /> Mood: Exhausting and Desperate<br /> Fun tidbits: Germanic Africans, Berbers, religious tensions amongst the Catholics &amp; Arianist Christians, the oncoming Byzantine invasion.<br /> <br /> Too bad that doesn't help you, life and death go on. But it isn't easy and dangers abound. Life has never been easy here, not in 3000 years. Even now the rest of the world feels far away. Worse, as long people keep dying, they keep endangering the living. Some secrets beneath the sands &amp; waves calls to them, be it ancient gods or dark spirits.<br /> From such shadows, the dead live again. Some are called, others pledge themselves to death itself. Fate has decreed that the living must be tested.<br /> <br /> King Hilderic the Heretic has been cast from his throne. Long live King Gelimer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T19:06:47-07:00","id":437882,"title":"","content":"On the Hunter page, I suggested the Fifteenth Century failure or loss of the Norse colonies in Greenland. I feel there are so many interesting possibilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/426532-greenland-lost-hunter-dark-era-idea\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/426532-greenland-lost-hunter-dark-era-idea\"> Greenland Lost (Hunter Dark Era idea) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/426532-greenland-lost-hunter-dark-era-idea\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/426532-greenland-lost-hunter-dark-era-idea </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Starting in the Tenth Century, Vikings settled the southern part of Greenland, In the Thirteenth Century, Inuit (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inuit) peoples joined </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T20:34:22-07:00","id":437959,"title":"","content":"Enough of me being negative, it's time I posted some of my ideas.<br /> <br /> Setting: Germany, 1626\u20131631 AD<br /> Game line: Vampire/Werewolf Crossover<br /> <br /> Between 1626 and 1631, the Bamberg and W\u00fcrzburg witch trials took place. This all went on at the same time and area as the 30 Years' War, which was one of the most devastating wars in the history of Europe. Now I know Hunter or the Possessed from Inferno are the obvious choice (or Giest if you want to focus on the war itself), but that is why I would rather see what depravity the Bale Hounds and Belial's Brood would get up to in a time like this. It would be interesting to see how these two similar groups would interact with each other. Outside of that, massive Wounds would be forming which would be a huge problem for werewolves and I don't think we've ever seen how vampires deal with such brutal wars. This war was heavily fueled by hostility between Lutherans and Catholics, so it would be interesting to see what effect this would have on the Lancea et Sanctum, which would have largely been made up of former Catholics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T12:20:45-07:00","id":438765,"title":"","content":"Updated the Wheels within Wheels pitch in the OP based on feedback. Please let me know what you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T22:03:19-07:00","id":439377,"title":"","content":"My personal preference is not go to any definitive answers like that about any major world religion. But if it works for your table that's great, but I know it goes against the NWoD ethos in handling these topics in canon printed material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T22:05:43-07:00","id":439379,"title":"","content":"You have convinced me to use Demon for the Babylonian Captivity though, and make that a Demon/Promethean crossover instead of Vampire/Promethean (which we're already getting with the 14th Century Black Death) - I'll just have vampires play a background threat role (drawing on Ancient Bloodlines), but not be major players in the setting's central God-Machine vs. Principle conflict (which do not break along national lines).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:19:22-07:00","id":439491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=439379#post439379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have convinced me to use Demon for the Babylonian Captivity though, and make that a Demon/Promethean crossover instead of Vampire/Promethean (which we're already getting with the 14th Century Black Death) - I'll just have vampires play a background threat role (drawing on Ancient Bloodlines), but not be major players in the setting's central God-Machine vs. Principle conflict (which do not break along national lines).</div> </div> </div> </div>Suppose that backstory is just the mythology of the Israelite Awakened and there's no actual proof ...?<br /> <br /> Honestly, the setting is rich enough that it can support all the splats IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T00:33:15-07:00","id":439555,"title":"","content":"Anyone have any ideas for non-Egyptian pre-Colonial African Eras? I like the idea of the Mansa Musa Pilgrimage as a focal point, but I'm not sure what to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:41:47-07:00","id":440129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=439555#post439555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have any ideas for non-Egyptian pre-Colonial African Eras? I like the idea of the Mansa Musa Pilgrimage as a focal point, but I'm not sure what to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in case you don't already have one, here's a list of pre-Colonial African kingdoms.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_kingdoms_in_pre-colonial_Africa\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of...olonial_Africa</a><br /> <br /> I'll skim over a few and see if anything jumps out and screams &quot;World of Darkness plot hooks!&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Carthage circa the Second Punic Wars sounds pretty interesting. It's close enough to Egypt that you could get some Mummy action going, and of course the conflict with Rome lets you work the Camarilla in there. Numidia would also be in the same region at the same time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carthaginian_Empire\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Carthage_264bc.svg/1280px-Carthage_264bc.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carthaginian_Empire\" target=\"_blank\"> Ancient Carthage - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carthaginian_Empire\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carthaginian_Empire </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Numidia\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Monnaie_-_Bronze%2C_Incertain%2C_Numidie%2C_Massinissa_-_btv1b84804368_%282_of_2%29.jpg/1280px-Monnaie_-_Bronze%2C_Incertain%2C_Numidie%2C_Massinissa_-_btv1b84804368_%282_of_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Numidia\" target=\"_blank\"> Numidia - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Numidia\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Numidia </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Oooh. <i>Engage comparative religion/mythology geekery </i>The high muckety-muck god of the Carthaginian pantheon was <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baal-hamon\" target=\"_blank\">Baal-Hamon</a>, which has obvious phonetic similarities to the Egyptian deity Amon and the angel Amoniel of Lancea et Sanctum mythology. Amon, of course, was assimilated with Zeus as Zeus-Ammon by the Greeks. And his consort was Tanit, possibly cognate with Egyptian tA-Newet, &quot;tA&quot; meaning &quot;Earth&quot; and Newet being Nut, the sky goddess, so a rough translation would be &quot;Earth-Sky&quot; or &quot;Earth-Heaven&quot;, which has some interesting parallels in Sumerian mythology via the primordial couple Anshar and Kishar (Carthage was a Phoenician culture, which ties it to Mesopotamia). Or possibly TAw-Newet, &quot;Breath of Nut/Breath of the Heavens,&quot; which has possible connections to Hebrew beliefs (Genesis 1:1-2 references the creation of the heavens and the earth and says that the &quot;ruach&quot;, which means both &quot;spirit&quot; and &quot;breath&quot;, of God, brooded on the face of the waters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-13-2015, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:04:45-07:00","id":440269,"title":"","content":"1906 San Francisco Earthquake - Promethean<br /> <br /> In the terrible aftermath of this terrible event, the Created ask themselves if they were the cause of ruin of the San Francisco, the Paris of the West. Alas, sweeping fires and other challenges give the city's prometheans little time for reflection.<br /> <br /> Bonus: fits fairly nicely between the Year without Summer and the Dust Bowl.<br /> <br /> I by (happy) accident bought a Promethean book. This might very well be the game that I play with it when I get the chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:41:27-07:00","id":440621,"title":"","content":"Just for the hell of it:<br /> <br /> In the Name of Progress:<br /> <br /> Gameline: Genius<br /> <br /> Period: Industrial Revolution<br /> <br /> Smog fills the sky, as mankind reaches a new dawn. Agricultural output is at an all-time high, financial backing is easier to get than ever, and new machines have created cheap, easily manufactured goods. The rapid advancement has a dark side: exploitation of man and mineral threaten to rip the heart and soul out of the United States and Europe. On top of all that, Geniuses are Catalyzing at an unprecedented rate, reinvigorating the old conflicts between the Lemurians and the Peerage. Will you join the Lemurians, plundering the wealth of the era at the expense of the people, or will you stand to defend the common man alongside the Peerage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:22:38-07:00","id":440856,"title":"","content":"Tell you what, I'll make a list of my ideas, and you guys pick which one you'd like more details on (some of these are inspired by pitches from the Kickstarter)<br /> <br /> - Book of Judges Hunter/Mummy<br /> - Vedic Demon<br /> - Babylonian Captivity Demon/Promethean<br /> - Qin Dynasty Vampire (+ Immortals)<br /> - Camelot Mage/Changeling<br /> - Islamic Golden Age Changeling<br /> - Haudenosaunee Hunter<br /> - 14th Century Italy Geist/Inferno<br /> - Incan Mummy<br /> - 17th Century English Promethean<br /> - Golden Age of Piracy Mage/Geist<br /> - French Revolution Mage<br /> - 1830s India Vampire/Hunter<br /> - Antebellum Geist<br /> - Wild West Demon<br /> - Meiji Restoration Werewolf/Changeling<br /> - Turn of the Century Himalayas/Mongolia Beast<br /> - Great War Werewolf<br /> - Jazz Age Vampire/Beast<br /> - WW2 Hunter","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T00:30:52-07:00","id":441053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=440856#post440856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell you what, I'll make a list of my ideas, and you guys pick which one you'd like more details on (some of these are inspired by pitches from the Kickstarter)<br /> <br /> - Book of Judges Hunter/Mummy<br /> - Babylonian Captivity Demon/Promethean</div> </div> </div> </div>These 2 interest me greatly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T00:41:41-07:00","id":441063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=440856#post440856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell you what, I'll make a list of my ideas, and you guys pick which one you'd like more details on (some of these are inspired by pitches from the Kickstarter)<br /> <br /> - Vedic Demon<br /> - Qin Dynasty Vampire (+ Immortals)<br /> - Camelot Mage/Changeling<br /> - Islamic Golden Age Changeling<br /> - Haudenosaunee Hunter<br /> - Incan Mummy<br /> - Meiji Restoration Werewolf/Changeling<br /> - Jazz Age Vampire/Beast</div> </div> </div> </div>Incan Mummy has me tickled pink, and I'd to see how your Meiji Era differs from mine. The rest are just gravy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T07:05:02-07:00","id":441259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=440856#post440856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell you what, I'll make a list of my ideas, and you guys pick which one you'd like more details on (some of these are inspired by pitches from the Kickstarter)<br /> <br /> - Vedic Demon<br /> - Babylonian Captivity Demon/Promethean<br /> - Camelot Mage/Changeling<br /> - 14th Century Italy Geist/Inferno<br /> - Incan Mummy<br /> - Golden Age of Piracy Mage/Geist<br /> - French Revolution Mage<br /> - 1830s India Vampire/Hunter<br /> - Antebellum Geist<br /> - Wild West Demon<br /> - Meiji Restoration Werewolf/Changeling<br /> - Turn of the Century Himalayas/Mongolia Beast<br /> - Great War Werewolf<br /> - Jazz Age Vampire/Beast<br /> - WW2 Hunter</div> </div> </div> </div>These all seem neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T23:13:45-07:00","id":453888,"title":"","content":"Beast the Primordial in Book of Invasions Ireland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T23:17:22-07:00","id":453893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=435904#post435904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. So here's a thought. According to the Testament of Marco Singe-</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it's occurred to you or if someone brought it up, but I'm gonna mention that there's a high probability Marco Singe <i>was fucking insane</i>.<br /> <br /> I mean, hell, we already know now he was fundamentally wrong on one major score.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:53:23-07:00","id":454194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=453888#post453888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast the Primordial in Book of Invasions Ireland.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast in pre-revolutionary France. What do you think the Wolf of Gevaudan was?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:16:06-07:00","id":454452,"title":"","content":"Beasts have claimed an island nation for themselves, and things are looking pretty good for them until a tribe of divine heroes come to wage war with them. It's a time when it seems like Beasts have finally won out over the cycle of violence only to be rebuked by some of the most potent heroes. It's the death of a primal, mystic age with sky-clad druids, hidden lands and islands, and creatures who defy classifications being united under the Fomorians and the Tuatha De Danann. Alternatively could be pushed to the end of the Book of Invasions when not heroes but simple migration ends an era, with the Milesians conquering Ireland(Although I think that might work better as a Changeling story, and I want to avoid obvious Changeling-Ireland connections just because it's too easy[though I would still love doing it]), or even during the Ulster cycle at some point (Since there's theories that it's pseudo-set around the time of Christ, although that's probably the result of Christian monks).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-23-2015, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T21:52:20-07:00","id":455401,"title":"","content":"I'll get to posting my pitches shortly but I ended up having to tinker with a couple...<br /> <br /> I realized the Antebellum US should really be Changeling rather than Geist, since the central element of the narrative will be the escape from slavery.<br /> <br /> However, that ends up contemporary with another slavery-focused Changeling Era idea: The Dahomey vs. Abeotuka conflict. It's a good niche for Changeling with the founding of a new safe haven from the slave trade.<br /> <br /> Preferences between focusing in on the Underground Railroad in the US, or Abeotuka casting off Dahomey power in Africa for Changeling? Do you think either work BETTER for some other gameline or combination there of (I was originally going to do the Underground Railroad as Geist, and play on the literal Autochthonous Depths)... I guess I could make Dahomey a Mummy/Changeling crossover since they have &quot;escape from slavery&quot; as a subtextual theme, even if (unlike Changelings) most of them don't even realize it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T05:48:07-07:00","id":455734,"title":"","content":"I'm personally leaning towards Changelings in the Antebellum(or even just plain bellum) Southern U.S. myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T06:54:50-07:00","id":455782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=455401#post455401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll get to posting my pitches shortly but I ended up having to tinker with a couple...<br /> <br /> I realized the Antebellum US should really be Changeling rather than Geist, since the central element of the narrative will be the escape from slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://24.media.tumblr.com/c4b8f12016e305d4b6d36ae8d7c5d3af/tumblr_mkws36UgVu1ry10fwo1_400.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> They could have done worse than to make Antebellum South the double chapter instead of Three Kingdoms China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T20:26:56-07:00","id":456526,"title":"","content":"Can we just do another Kickstarter and hire Glamourweaver to write a second Dark Eras book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T20:51:53-07:00","id":456544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=456526#post456526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we just do another Kickstarter and hire Glamourweaver to write a second Dark Eras book?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, I'd be really interested to see what a &quot;Dark Eras Fan Companion&quot; would look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T21:13:26-07:00","id":456552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=456526#post456526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we just do another Kickstarter and hire Glamourweaver to write a second Dark Eras book?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Someone else should do a Geist era, I'd help with the history side, but I don't LOVE GtSE enough to do it the justice it deserves (because it's in no way inferior, it just doesn't have my heart).<br /> <br /> I have decided on 3 Pre-Colombian settings for the hypothetical book (1 for North, South, and Central America each): in chronological order, the Fall of the Mayan Empire gets Mage; the birth of the Haudenosaunee (aka the Iroquois Confederation) gets Hunter; and the height of the Incan Empire gets Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:10:46-07:00","id":456941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=456552#post456552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Someone else should do a Geist era, I'd help with the history side, but I don't LOVE GtSE enough to do it the justice it deserves (because it's in no way inferior, it just doesn't have my heart).<br /> <br /> I have decided on 3 Pre-Colombian settings for the hypothetical book (1 for North, South, and Central America each): in chronological order, the Fall of the Mayan Empire gets Mage; the birth of the Haudenosaunee (aka the Iroquois Confederation) gets Hunter; and the height of the Incan Empire gets Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could do a Geist Era. After Promethean,it's my favorite line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:30:55-07:00","id":456965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=456544#post456544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, I'd be really interested to see what a &amp;quot;Dark Eras Fan Companion&amp;quot; would look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shit, I'm down for this. I don't know the games that well and my ideas might be more suited to non-interactive fiction than RPGs, but I can come up with a fuckton of concepts to throw at the wall and people can riff off whatever tickles their fancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:42:48-07:00","id":456977,"title":"","content":"I'd probably be totally useless, but I can at least try to give some ideas and feedback!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T10:10:24-07:00","id":457019,"title":"","content":"We should seriously do this. Should we start a new thread, or use this one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T11:11:40-07:00","id":457070,"title":"","content":"I think this one is fine as long as we're discussing era's conceptually - it's what the thread is already for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T11:33:13-07:00","id":457079,"title":"","content":"This one for planning, and a Google Doc or something for composing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T16:19:55-07:00","id":457400,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking what we should do is have a chapter per gameline to start, and have each chapter &quot;claimed&quot;/pitched by a different person. That way, we don't have one person trying to write a full book in their free time, plus we can have a wider variety of people and ideas going into this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T12:26:14-07:00","id":458251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=457400#post457400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking what we should do is have a chapter per gameline to start, and have each chapter &amp;quot;claimed&amp;quot;/pitched by a different person. That way, we don't have one person trying to write a full book in their free time, plus we can have a wider variety of people and ideas going into this.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about crossover eras? Heck, I'm thinking there are a few that have enough going on that they ought to be even MORE expansive than crossover eras. Something more like a blue book setting with extensive material on multiple game lines.<br /> <br /> For instance, the Babylonian Captivity is a great fit for Promethean, Demon, Mage, Vampire, Geist and possibly Hunter. So maybe Glamourweaver's Promethean/Demon concept is the main focus for that one, with extensive supplementary material regarding the other lines, written by other contributors. Here's what Mesopotamian Mage society is like, these are the myths of the Judean Awakened, check out some Sumerian-flavored Dead Dominions and a new Key, let's expand on the info in Ancient Mysteries/Ancient Bloodlines for Vampire, and by the way do you want a new Compact and some Tactics based off the Epic of Gilgamesh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T13:03:09-07:00","id":458286,"title":"","content":"I'm currently writing a Spanish Civl War Dark Era.<br /> <br /> It will have the following parts:<br /> - History: As in Requiem for Reqina. What has happened, what is happening now and what will happen.<br /> - Geography: The main spanish cities during second Republic and civil war, and their local Kinded<br /> - Factions: The main vampiric factions in the war: Covenants (includin two new ones: Libertarians and Phalanx of the Dead), Clans, Bloodlines (Cassians, Strigmeigas...) and local Ghoul Families (Matamoros)-<br /> - Systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T15:09:00-07:00","id":458373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=458286#post458286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently writing a Spanish Civl War Dark Era.<br /> <br /> It will have the following parts:<br /> - History: As in Requiem for Reqina. What has happened, what is happening now and what will happen.<br /> - Geography: The main spanish cities during second Republic and civil war, and their local Kinded<br /> - Factions: The main vampiric factions in the war: Covenants (includin two new ones: Libertarians and Phalanx of the Dead), Clans, Bloodlines (Cassians, Strigmeigas...) and local Ghoul Families (Matamoros)-<br /> - Systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>By any chance will you be willing/able to translate it? I can read some Spanish, so even sharing tidbits would be incredibly cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T17:22:16-07:00","id":458501,"title":"","content":"I plan to translate it to English. But I'll need help. Although I can read English as a native, I cannot write it as well.<br /> <br /> I'll ask help to an American friend. If he can't, I'll ask here too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T20:51:14-07:00","id":458635,"title":"","content":"As I'm assuming the Libertarians* correspond to the Republican* side of the human conflict, is there a specific reason they don't fall under the broader umbrella of the Carthians?<br /> <br /> *US Americans, neither of these words have the meaning here you'd think they do if you're making assumptions off of US politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T21:06:53-07:00","id":458646,"title":"","content":"OK, so as far as pitches we have:<br /> <br /> Meiji Japan (Werewolf) -Atamajakki<br /> Colonial Africa (Mage) - Lostlight<br /> London Blitz (Vampire) - Nifara<br /> Rise of Islam (Vampire) - Nifara<br /> 22nd Century Mars (Changeling/Geist) - Rayungoth<br /> Ancient Sumeria (Mummy/Immortals) - Malonkey1<br /> Vandalic War-era Carthage (Geist/Mummy) - FallenEco<br /> Fifteenth Century Greenland (Hunter) - Cire<br /> 30 Years' War Germany (Vampire/Werewolf)<br /> 1906 San Francisco Earthquake (Promethean) - Cire<br /> Babylonian Captivity (Crossover, game lines TBD; likely either Promethean/Demon with possible supplementary material or World of Darkness/God-Machine Chronicles with extensive line-specific notes and sidebars) - Glamourweaver or Xenu's Paradox<br /> <br /> Additional Eras (TBD) - Glamourweaver<br /> <br /> I'm not counting Genius (fansplat) or Beast (unreleased).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-27-2015, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T22:25:19-07:00","id":458674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=458635#post458635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I'm assuming the Libertarians* correspond to the Republican* side of the human conflict, is there a specific reason they don't fall under the broader umbrella of the Carthians?<br /> <br /> *US Americans, neither of these words have the meaning here you'd think they do if you're making assumptions off of US politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're partially right. They are an split of Carthians. In my original idea, they were a radical Carthian faction, and I wrote originally in this way in land of the Damned: Spain. But with Requiem 2d edition, which gives more freedom in the covenant system, I converted them in a independent covenant (although split from carthians).<br /> <br /> They are the vampire version of the internal divisions and infightings of the Republican side, in which socialists and comunists were in a inner war against anarchists and trotskists. They splintered after some internal Carthian fightings about the failed attempt of create a Carthian Republic in Spain.<br /> <br /> And yes, they could fall under the broader Carthian Umbrella, but the hatred among both Carthian factons is so high, that thay work in practice as an independent covenant.<br /> <br /> *Yes, in Spain, Libertarians is a term synonim of anarchist, a meaning very different than in America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T21:36:11-07:00","id":459669,"title":"","content":"Chrome ate my post.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm working on a Vampire era set in classical Greece on the eve of the Second Persian Invasion. Elysia are a recent innovation, offering foreigners a safe place to plea their case and staunch Kindred politicians an arena to debate until frenzy. It also features an empire-building Strix that is obsessed with burning Athens to the ground.<br /> <br /> Some early drafts made it in my Actual Play thread. Will definitely be posting a lot more after I'm done with my final year in college.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T09:05:22-07:00","id":890599,"title":"","content":"I know this is a necro, but I really want to see a Dark Eras fan companion happen. The issue is, I don't know where to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T09:18:20-07:00","id":890603,"title":"","content":"I gave some initial development of both a Spanish Inquisition and a Book of Judges Eras, and I have some thoughts about a Punic Wars as an Hunter/Demon Crossover Era. Maybe I'll also work on Colonial Africa Era for Mage later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:48:28-07:00","id":890723,"title":"","content":"<b>The Weimar Republic (Interregnum Germany)</b> - Social liberties, crushing debt, and the rise of Fascism. (Werewolf/Hunter)<br /> <br /> World War I just happened - due to some <i>bad choices</i> made by Kaiser Wilhelm II, it's officially Germany's fault. And the rest of Europe <i>won't</i> let them forget it.<br /> <br /> The traditional leadership is <i>gone</i>, France is occupying the industrial centres along the Rhine, and the population is facing <i>crippling</i> debt and inflation due to the rest of Europe demanding reparations. Germany's national pride is gone, but...<br /> <br /> There's no censorship. Prostitution for both sexes is legal, homosexuality isn't criminalized, and women had the vote.Germany took a <i>massive</i> step forward for the arts and film. But...<br /> <br /> No one <i>wanted</i> a democracy - it had a built-in &quot;go back to autocracy&quot; clause in the constitution. The government was divided and weak; there were paramilitary gangs of young men wandering the countryside, since the military didn't have a place for them. Near the end, you had Communists and National Socialists getting into bloody skirmishes in the streets.<br /> <br /> It was a disaster waiting to happen - and we all know how it ends.<br /> <br /> But they didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T13:57:55-07:00","id":890777,"title":"","content":"If I ever get a few days off work, I'd love to actually develop my 1960s America Mage setting, All Along The Watchtowers. It plays off similar themes as Mage Noir, with the idea that America as a nation has Awakened - and possibly broken in the face of the truth. Vietnam is a war with incredibly low public support, a source of dead brothers and horrific images on the television rather than the patriotic glories of the past. Social conservatism and mainstream religion ring utterly false to the young and the famous, who increasingly toy with free love, hard drugs, and fringe religions (that in the Chronicles of Darkness world may well be genuinely supernatural). Race relations and generational gaps threaten to boil over into blood in the streets. Sleepers breach the heavens and walk on the face of the moon, something well beyond even the greatest magic of Masters.<br /> <br /> The reality of the Fallen World rings increasingly hollow, but it seems like the Sleepers would sooner spiral into madness than find the Supernal lurking underneath. It's Cold War paranoia and Hollywood cult murders and acid trips bringing fragile minds into contact with alien intelligences. It's magic being increasingly invalidated by technology and new symbols overtaking the old faster than anyone can comprehend. <br /> <br /> It may well be the apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T15:00:55-07:00","id":890826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=439555#post439555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have any ideas for non-Egyptian pre-Colonial African Eras? I like the idea of the Mansa Musa Pilgrimage as a focal point, but I'm not sure what to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fulani Jihad, and rise of the Sokoto Caliphate, works for several lines. In the early 19th Century, members of the Fulani ethnic group conquered a series of Hausa city-states in (what's now) Nigeria. History remembers the Jihad as springing from a mix of ethnic tension, religious* intolerance, and a desire for social reform; sparked by the exile of the religious scholar Uthman dan Fodio. But who says history is right?<br /> <br /> The Fulani Jihad could easily have been cover for a feud between vampires. Or mages. Perhaps the Hausa city-states were strongholds of the Diamond, and the jihadis pawns of the Exarchs (possibly Paternoster). Or maybe it was the other way 'round, with abusive Seers in charge, and the Jihad was a revolt by African chapters of the Adamantite Arrow and various Nameless groups (one of the frequent charges was that the Hausa leaders had lost touch with their spiritual beliefs . . . )<br /> <br /> Not hard to see werewolves, or Beasts, or hunters getting in on the action, either. Or maybe the truth was that the Unchained cut one too many deals with the Hausa rulers, and caught the eye of the God-Machine . .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * <i>Despite technically being Muslim, Hausa rulers allowed (or at least turned a blind eye towards) the practice of traditional African religions, which outraged the more orthodox revolutionaries . </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T18:30:44-07:00","id":890897,"title":"","content":"Can All Along the Watchtowers be set in San Francisco?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T18:42:28-07:00","id":890905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=890897#post890897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can All Along the Watchtowers be set in San Francisco?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was gonna be that or Los Angeles, but the Mage 2e core laying down canon material for LA probably means we're going to the Bay Area. One of my uncles swears he smoked some dope with one of the Manon family up there.<br /> <br /> All Along The Watchtowers has a dedicated thread over in the Mage forum, BTW. I'd love for it to be a collab setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T19:27:15-07:00","id":890921,"title":"","content":"I thought about reviving it from page 3 a couple days ago but I'm only just now <i>really</i> digging into The Sundered World so I'm mentally out of commission for anything else.<br /> <br /> Well, except <b>Deviant</b> but that's because the new season of Orphan Black is on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T08:53:05-07:00","id":891173,"title":"","content":"<b>Hunter: Manifest Destiny</b><br /> <br /> Hunters in the Post-Bellum United States. Taking on Victorian Vampires and geniuses in the choked and polluted cities, werewolves and fae in the expansive plains, and all the human magics in between.<br /> <br /> With a little more detail, the 1860s-1890s was when the US really went into overdrive on taking the plains and united the coasts. With the completion of the Transcontinental Railroad and the advancements in ship building technology the United States was taking the continent by storm. Hunters would inevitably spring up when facing the werewolves trying to destroy the railroads and mines springing up, the strange and secretive esoteric societies rising among the middle and upper classes in the cities, mad scientists trying to force their inventions of the unwilling and unknowing public, along with any fearsome critters found during the expansion. Firearms technology was advanced to the point of repeating fire with self-contained cartridges, and the hunter concepts stretch from Native Americans trying to protect their ways of life, to immigrants carrying with them the secrets of their homelands, to American-born citizens finding out about what lurks in their cities and settlements. The game can take place in the classic &quot;Old West&quot; boom town or ghost town, across the Great Plains, the bustling coastal cities, the lumber camps of the Northwest, isolated reservations and Federal forts, and the few remaining tribal settlements left. Perhaps even a mission to Alaska and Hawai'i?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T03:17:18-07:00","id":891647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/433319-elevator-pitch-a-dark-era?p=439555#post439555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have any ideas for non-Egyptian pre-Colonial African Eras? I like the idea of the Mansa Musa Pilgrimage as a focal point, but I'm not sure what to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some more options, besides the Fulani Jihad: <br /> <br /> The history (and mythological baggage) of Ethiopia lends itself to a Mage &amp; Changeling setting. Medieval Europeans sort of knew it was there, telling stories of the kingdom of Prester John, a Christian civilization lost somewhere in Africa. Its just that sometimes they seem to be talking about a real place, and sometimes a fantasy land. Home to one of the oldest forms of Christianity in the world (Ethiopia's overwhelmingly Coptic Christian), and yet cut off from the rest of Christendom, it could well be a magnet for medieval mages looking for &quot;lost&quot; mysteries. And some might find more than they expected, stumbling upon the faerie kingdom of the &quot;real&quot; Prester John.<br /> <br /> For more recent events, you could look at the invasion of the Galla, or Ethiopia's defeat of Italy. That's right, during the colonial era, Ethiopia actually defeated the European power seeking to colonize it.<br /> <br /> Or, if you want more of a blank slate, there's Meroe (pronounced &quot;mare-oh-way&quot;). Located in what is now northern and South Sudan, it started out as an ancient Egyptian colony known as &quot;Kush&quot;, and later gained <i>de facto</i> independence during internal strife in ancient Egypt. However, almost overnight, for no obvious reason, it turns into the kingdom of Meroe. The language shifts dramatically, to the point that modern scholars are still struggling to translate it, and lion imagery suddenly becomes very prominent. Meroe survived into the Fourth Century AD . . . when it just sort of disappeared. <br /> <br /> Obviously, that gives you a lot of flexibility. A civilization that radically changes, for no good reason, flourishes for a thousand years, and then just . . . stops. Again, for no obvious reason. There are a thousand cool things you could do with any of the splats, regarding the rise and fall of Meroe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}